    "text": "Branwen is a woman of the Welsh stories. She was the child of Llyr. Her brother was the hero Brân the Blessed. She belongs to the second branch of the Mabinogion. She was given as a bride to a king of Ireland. The king was called Matholwch, and Ireland was his land. Her kinsman Efnisien struck at the Irish by harming their horses. Grief came for Branwen in her time there. She died, and they say she looked like the goddess Rhiannon in her sorrow.",
